.TH MYSTRCPY 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mystrcpy \- copy a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.PP
.BI "int mystrcpy(char *" dest ", const char *" src );
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mystrcpy()
function copies the string pointed to by
.IR src ,
including the terminating null byte, to the buffer pointed to by
.IR dest .
The destination buffer must be large enough to hold the result.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters copied (excluding the null byte),
or \-1 if either pointer is NULL.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mystrncpy (3),
.BR mystrlen (3)
